---
Find the smallest circle on the globe containing a given share of world population, by great-circle radius rather than by area on a projected map.

Usage: popcircles [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  distance            Great-circle distance between two coordinates, in kilometres
  grid                Raster grid geometry
  country             List the registered country identifiers and names
  table               The summation table and its on-disk cache
  population-at       The population inside a circle of a given ground radius about a coordinate
  most-populous       The most populous circle of a fixed ground radius, over every cell centre of the grid
  smallest-for-share  The smallest circle whose population reaches a share of the table's own total
  sweep               The smallest circle for each of a range of shares, over one ledger
  help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --log-level <LEVEL>  How much to report on stderr: `error`, `warn`, `info` or `debug`. It does not govern the progress meter, which answers how far a run has got rather than what happened [default: info]
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version
